      "description": "•Create, maintain and update departmental websites and applications accessed and used University-wide, spanning 24 campuses across the city’s five boroughs.\n•Work with cross functional teams (UI/UX Designers, Backend Developers) to develop and update user interfaces for various applications and forms using HTML5, CSS3, Javascript, jQuery\n•Implementing UI/UX design protocols to create a more streamlined user experience\n•Adding dynamic functions to existing and new web applications (client side validation, custom form controls and behavior, etc.) \n•Conversion of static websites to responsive layouts that adapt to various devices (desktops, laptops, mobile devices, etc.) using CSS media queries and CSS frameworks such as Bootstrap and Foundation\nTest for cross browser compatibility issues (Chrome DevTools)\n•Implement web page optimization techniques for improved and fast loading times (minify css and javascript, image compression) \n•Work with Graphic Design teams to create pixel perfect images optimized for view on various devices using Image editing software (Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, etc.) \n•Build responsive email templates compatible with email clients; used for distribution of information in regard to upcoming application upgrades and available resources for faculty, students, and staff\n•Conduct training on the use of website content management systems \n•Conduct accessibility compliance audits on websites, web based applications, software applications, Mobile apps, PDF documents and forms, Microsoft Word docs, Power Point presentations\n•Accessibility Evaluation – WCAG 2.0 & WCAG 2.1 (Level A, AA, AAA) , ATAG, Section 508 & UAAG\n•Applied knowledge of WAI-ARIA Concepts\n•Accessibility Testing Tools – Assistive technologies (screen readers -JAWS & NVDA), Keyboard, Browser •Automated Testing, Color Contrast Analyzer",
